    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d275-a1">

                <pb facs="0781" n="743" xml:id="pg743"/>

                <head>Annex 1</head>
                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#bold">Letter From the Deputy Secretary of
                        Defense (Robertson) to the British Permanent Secretary at the Ministry of
                        Defence (Powell)<anchor n="6" xml:id="d275-f1"/></hi></p>
                <p rendition="#right"><hi rendition="#italic">Bermuda, March 23, 1957.</hi></p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear Sir Richard</hi>: I attach
                    hereto Memoranda of Conversation covering two of the topics which were discussed
                    at the meeting yesterday afternoon which the Prime Minister, the Foreign
                    Secretary and yourself had with the President, Secretary Dulles, Secretary Quarles, Admiral Strauss
                    and myself.</p>
                <p>I am able to confirm to you that the attached memoranda represent the
                    understandings of the United States side in these matters.</p>
                <p>I should be grateful if you could confirm to me that they also represent the
                    understandings of the United Kingdom side.</p>
                <p>Sincerely yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Reuben B.
                                Robertson</hi><anchor n="7" xml:id="d275-f2"
                    /></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
